<article class="env-remark" id="0G4G">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G4G">Remark <span data-tag="0G4G">37.32.4</span>.</a> Let us sketch a “geometric” proof of a special case of Lemma <a href="/tag/0G4F" data-tag="0G4F">37.32.3</a>. Namely, say $k$ is an algebraically closed field and $X \subset \mathbf{P}^ n_ k$ is smooth and irreducible of dimension $\geq 2$. Then we claim there is a hyperplane $H \subset \mathbf{P}^ n_ k$ such that $X \cap H$ is smooth and irreducible. Namely, by Varieties, Lemma <a href="/tag/0FD6" data-tag="0FD6">33.47.3</a> for a general $v \in V = kT_0 \oplus \ldots \oplus kT_ n$ the corresponding hyperplane section $X \cap H_ v$ is smooth. On the other hand, by Enriques-Severi-Zariski the scheme $X \cap H_ v$ is connected, see Varieties, Lemma <a href="/tag/0FD9" data-tag="0FD9">33.48.3</a>. Hence $X \cap H_ v$ is smooth and irreducible. </p>
